AB  - A technique is described for the accurate measurement of angular errors using photoelectric detectors. Utilizing two types of rugged, compact cartridges, a wide range of characteristic curves may be synthesized. Examples of various systems are shown, including one for a high accuracy servo. The latter has a coverage of 360 degrees, a null accuracy of one minute, and is in current use in Aerobee Rockets.
